error[NK1206]: A `for` can't walk `foo`: a `Foo` holds no elements.
   --> tests/a_for_over_what_holds_no_elements_is_refused.nika:15:5
    |
 15 |     for l in foo {
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `foo` is a `Foo`, which holds no elements: a `for` walks a sequence, a range, a list, a set, a map or what a call produces (Part I 3.3).
    = help: Walk a list the `Foo` holds, `for … in foo.<field> { … }`, or put the values in a list first.
